 "answers": {
  "Q1": {
   "answer": "The paper addresses fragmentation in the infrastructure for building and evaluating LLM-based agents that act through software. Existing frameworks each solve only part of the problem (multi-agent chat, or SWE-only, or web-only) and none combines safe sandboxed code execution, extensible tools, multi-agent delegation, and broad systematic evaluation, making cross-approach comparison and progress measurement hard.",
