   "confidence": 5,
   "missing": ""
  },
  "Q2": {
   "answer": "Software (code execution, shell, browsers) is how skilled humans interact with digital systems and is expressive (Turing-complete) and deterministic, so it is well-suited as a universal action space for agents; but the tooling to build/evaluate such agents is immature, motivating a unified open platform.",
   "locations": [
    "\u00a71 paras 2-4",
    "\u00a72 Background"
   ],
   "confidence": 5,
   "missing": ""
  },
  "Q3": {
   "answer": "Implicit research question: Can a single generalist agent using code as its primary action space achieve competitive performance across distinct task categories (software engineering, web browsing, general assistance) without task-specific modification, and can shared open infrastructure support such evaluation? The paper never states an explicit hypothesis.",
   "locations": [
    "\u00a71 (contributions)",
    "\u00a77 Discussion para 1"
   ],
   "confidence": 3,
   "missing": "No explicitly framed research question or hypothesis statement."
  },
  "Q4": {
   "answer": "Primary contribution is the OpenHands open platform providing shared agent infrastructure. Secondary: (1) event-stream architecture decoupling agent logic from execution, (2) Docker-sandboxed runtime for safe code execution on arbitrary images, (3) extensible AgentSkills library, (4) multi-agent delegation, (5) unified 15-benchmark evaluation framework. Plus the empirical demonstration via CodeActAgent.",
   "locations": [
    "\u00a71 (numbered list + Contributions)",
    "Abstract"
   ],
   "confidence": 5,
   "missing": ""
  },
  "Q5": {
   "answer": "An agent is a step function mapping state (an event stream of past action-observation pairs) to the next typed action (IPythonRunCell, CmdRun, BrowseInteractive, Message, AgentDelegate). Actions run inside a per-session Docker container exposing a REST execution API with a persistent bash shell, Jupyter kernel, and Playwright Chromium. AgentSkills adds utilities only when LLMs reliably fail or an external model is needed. CodeActAgent acts primarily by generating executable code.",
   "locations": [
    "\u00a73.1-\u00a73.4",
    "\u00a74 Agent Hub"
   ],
   "confidence": 5,
   "missing": ""
  },
  "Q6": {
